{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c001", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The parenthetical \"(“Agreement”) as further defined below.”\" is garbled by a stray quotation mark and promises a definition of \"Agreement\" that the instrument never supplies. Whether \"Agreement\" includes the exhibits and successor forms is left to Section 15(vii) rather than settled here.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.11}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The sentence that \"neither party shall in any event be held liable or accountable for any obligations incurred by either party other than as specified herein\" cannot easily be squared with the mutual indemnity in Section 13(i), which makes each party answerable for losses caused by its own acts and omissions. Which of the two governs claims for a party's obligations to third parties is unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.15}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"[T]hose products authorized by COMPANY for sale to DISTRIBUTOR\" fixes no list, writing or other means by which authorization is shown, so the content of PRODUCTS floats. Combined with COMPANY's right to eliminate any PRODUCT \"for any reason,\" the subject matter of the agreement is indeterminate.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The definition confines the AUTHORIZED CHANNEL OF TRADE to \"retail grocery store outlet customers only,\" which cannot be squared with Section 3(ii)(a)(i), permitting sales to Kmart and to \"specific customers as approved by COMPANY,\" or with Exhibit B's statement that DISTRIBUTOR may distribute to Kmart. Whether Kmart sales are inside or outside the authorized channel (and so a termination ground under Section 12(iii)(a)) is left open.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.33}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"[S]tandards that have developed and are universally accepted and followed in the baking industry\" is a vague benchmark, and \"universally accepted\" sets a threshold no practice plausibly meets. Because failure to follow Good Industry Practice is a termination ground under Section 12(iii)(b), the content of the term matters and is unfixed.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.29}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c006", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"[S]hall continue for until December 31, 2008\" and \"or until terminates in accordance with paragraph |2 herein\" are grammatically broken, leaving unclear whether the agreement simply expires on that date or continues until terminated. The mechanical errors change the meaning of the term.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.40},
    {"issue": "The final sentence lets either party terminate on ninety days' written notice after December 31, 2008 without any stated cause, while Section 12(i) permits ninety-day termination only \"for good cause\" or on a change in COMPANY's business. The two cannot both be given effect.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.44}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c007", "issues": [
    {"issue": "COMPANY's power to \"determine the TERRITORY and AUTHORIZED CHANNEL OF TRADE\" during the term conflicts with Section I(iii) and Exhibit A, which fix TERRITORY by a written designation, and with Section 15(iii), permitting modification only by a written instrument executed by both parties. Whether COMPANY can shrink the territory unilaterally is left unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.27}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c008", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"[S]pecific customers as approved by COMPANY\" specifies no form or manner of approval, so whether oral approval or course of dealing suffices is open. The enumerated permissions (grocery outlets, Kmart) sit against this open-ended third category.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c009", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The in-store services \"will consist of, but are not limited to\" four listed activities, so the catch-all leaves the scope of the service obligation unbounded beyond the enumerated specifics. What further duties the phrase imports is a matter of construction.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.23}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c010", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The closing sentence — \"DISTRIBUTOR must meet certain other guidelines that the COMPANY may determine in its discretion from time to time\" — is an unbounded catch-all appended to two specific prohibitions (wholesaler operations and bid processes). Neither the guidelines nor any notice of them is identified.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c011", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The duty to adhere to standards, policies and procedures \"as shall from time to time be promulgated, altered, amended or modified by COMPANY\" lets COMPANY change DISTRIBUTOR's obligations unilaterally, which conflicts with Section 15(iii) permitting modification only by a written instrument executed by both parties. Which provision controls a policy change is unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.31}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c012", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"DISTRIBUTOR shall not sell the PRODUCTS ... to any CUSTOMERS or in any AUTHORIZED CHANNEL OF TRADE other than as stated herein\" is mis-drafted: read literally it forbids sales in the very channel the agreement authorizes. The mechanical error changes the meaning of the prohibition.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26},
    {"issue": "The flat prohibition on selling to customers and channels listed on Exhibit “B” cannot be squared with the closing paragraph of Exhibit B, which permits DISTRIBUTOR to continue selling to and servicing its existing customers falling within that schedule until further notice. Whether legacy excluded-channel customers are a breach turns on which text controls.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c013", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The duty to use \"commercially reasonable efforts to resolve any conflicts\" is triggered only by sales \"in conflict with Paragraph 3(a)(i) above,\" a paragraph number that does not exist in this agreement (the customer list is Section 3(ii)(a)(i)). The miscitation leaves unclear which sales trigger COMPANY's obligation.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28}
